    <DataNode elementId="AT1G75330-MONOMER" textLabel="AT1G75330-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9FWS2" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="415" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The cDNA encoding for ornithine carbamoyltransferase (OTC) has been identified from a T-DNA-tagged mutant. This mutant is sensitive to ornithine which accumulates due to a partial loss of function of the mutant allele of the OTC gene. The OTC gene overlaps with another, unrelated gene (AUL1), one of the rare cases of gene convergence observed in &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; |CITS: [10561504]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G75330-MONOMER" />
